{title: There is a river}

{comment: Chorus}
There is a river, that follows from deep within.
There is a fountain, that frees the soul from sin.
Come to these waters; there is a vast supply.
There is a river, that never shall run dry.

{comment: Verse 1}
There came a sound from Heaven like a rushing, wind.
It filled their hearts with singing and gave them peace within.
The prophet gave this promise. He said, the Spirit will descend.
And from your inner being a river with no end.

{comment: Verse 2}
There came a thirsty woman, She was drawing from a well.
You see her life was ruined and wasted, and her soul was bound for hell.
Oh but then she met the Master who told of her great sin.
He said, “If you’ll just drink of this water, you’ll never thirst again”.
